Feature: Update volume paths in pyspark_script.py using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx

  The system must update only the volume paths in pyspark_script.py according to the mapping provided in volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx. All other script logic, structure, and variable names must remain unchanged.

  Background:
    Given the original pyspark_script.py contains hardcoded volume paths for biomarker_readings.csv, patient_demographics.csv, and site_details.csv
    And the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx (Sheet1) provides a one-to-one mapping of old_volume_path to new_volume_path for each CSV file
    And the script must not modify any logic, variable names, or processing steps except for the volume paths

  Scenario Outline: Update volume path for a CSV file as per mapping sheet
    Given the pyspark_script.py contains the line:
      """
      <read_line>
      """
    And the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains a mapping:
      | old_volume_path                                      | new_volume_path                                                        |
      | <old_volume_path>                                    | <new_volume_path>                                                      |
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then the corresponding line in pyspark_script.py must be replaced with:
      """
      <updated_read_line>
      """
    And no other part of the script is changed

    Examples:
      | read_line                                                                                                              | old_volume_path                                                                                   | new_volume_path                                                                                          | updated_read_line                                                                                                              |
      | biomarker_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv") | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv                | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv             | biomarker_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv") |
      | patient_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv") | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv               | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv  | patient_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv") |
      | site_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv")             | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv             | site_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv")             |

  Scenario: Do not update lines that do not match any old_volume_path in the mapping sheet
    Given the pyspark_script.py contains a line:
      """
      unrelated_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/other_volume/other_file.csv")
      """
    And the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx does not contain a mapping for "/Volumes/other_volume/other_file.csv"
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then the line remains unchanged

  Scenario: Error when mapping sheet is missing a required old_volume_path
    Given the pyspark_script.py contains a line:
      """
      biomarker_df = spark.read.option("header", True).csv("/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv")
      """
    And the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx does not contain a mapping for "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv"
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then the system must raise an error with message "Mapping for volume path '/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv' not found in mapping sheet."

  Scenario: Error when new_volume_path in mapping sheet is empty or null
    Given the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains a row with old_volume_path "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv" and new_volume_path ""
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then the system must raise an error with message "New volume path for '/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv' is empty or null in mapping sheet."

  Scenario: Validate that only the volume path is changed and all other script logic remains unchanged
    Given the pyspark_script.py contains logic for data cleaning, aggregation, joins, and display
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then only the volume paths for the three CSV files are changed as per the mapping
    And all other code, variable names, and logic remain exactly as in the original script

  Scenario: Validate the format of volume paths in mapping sheet
    Given the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains old_volume_path and new_volume_path values
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then each new_volume_path must start with "/Volumes/"
    And if any new_volume_path does not start with "/Volumes/", the system must raise an error with message "Invalid new volume path format for '<old_volume_path>': '<new_volume_path>'"

  Scenario: Validate that the mapping sheet contains no duplicate old_volume_path entries
    Given the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains multiple rows with the same old_volume_path
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then the system must raise an error with message "Duplicate old_volume_path '<old_volume_path>' found in mapping sheet."

  Scenario: Validate that the mapping sheet is read from Sheet1
    Given the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains multiple sheets
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then only mappings from Sheet1 are used for updating the script

  Scenario: Validate that the script is updated in-place and output is the complete updated code
    Given the pyspark_script.py is updated using the mapping sheet
    When the update is complete
    Then the output must be the complete code of pyspark_script.py with only the volume paths changed as per the mapping

